<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot name="wave_rover">

  <!--
    Waveshare UGV02 chassis. All dimensions measured in Session 013.
      chassis width   0.227 m
      chassis length  0.250 m
      track width     0.174 m   (front wheel contact patch to contact patch)
      lidar height    0.180 m   from floor
  -->

  <link name="base_link">
    <visual>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.250 0.227 0.100"/>
      </geometry>
    </visual>
  </link>

  <link name="laser">
    <visual>
      <geometry>
        <cylinder length="0.04" radius="0.03"/>
      </geometry>
    </visual>
  </link>

  <!--
    Session 013: yaw corrected from 0 to pi.
    The RPLidar C1 is mounted with its 0-bearing beam pointing toward the
    rover's REAR. Confirmed empirically: with a wall 3.00 m ahead and a
    second wall 0.113 m behind, /scan reported the 3 m surface as a
    coherent 38 deg arc spanning +/-180 deg, and the 0.113 m surface
    across the forward arc with a textbook 1/cos(theta) slant-range
    profile (agreement within 5 mm out to 55 deg).
    Previously rpy="0 0 0", which told the TF tree the laser faced
    forward. SLAM and RF2O were unaffected because every consumer was
    consistently wrong together, but Nav2 would have driven the rover
    backward along its planned path.

    FRAME CONVENTION (resolved Session 013): base_link sits at the
    chassis underside, the ground-clearance plane, 11.5 mm above the
    floor. The lidar measures 180 mm from the floor, so the joint offset
    is 180 - 11.5 = 168.5 mm. This recovers the provenance of the 0.1685
    value, which predates this session and had no recorded datum.

    Physical reference heights, for future measurements:
      chassis underside (= base_link)    11.5 mm from floor
      chassis mid-height                 45.0 mm from floor
      full-stack mid-height (Jetson)     90.0 mm from floor
      lidar plane                       180.0 mm from floor

    Lidar, IMU and Jetson are all centred over the chassis, so x and y
    offsets are zero by construction (confirmed Session 013).
  -->
  <joint name="base_to_laser" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="laser"/>
    <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 0.1685" rpy="0 0 3.14159265"/>
  </joint>

</robot>
